WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.404
- What do you think of my makeup?

00:00:01.404 --> 00:00:02.237
- Good.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.353
- Good?

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:05.150
Did you do a good job?

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.313
What part did you do?

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.793
Yeah?

00:00:08.793 --> 00:00:09.626
What else did you do?

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:10.883
My lipstick?

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.253
Wyatt did my lipstick.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:16.017
(cheery music)

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.640
^Hey guys, I'm Hannah, the world's OK-est mom

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.990
and welcome to my bathroom.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.487
If you're a busy parent like me, you know that mornings

00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:26.880
with kids are the most hectic time of day.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.950
I'm not paying attention to what I'm wearing or

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.763
how I even look as long as my kids have pants,

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:32.780
we're good to go.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.740
One thing I've heard is that if you want to try

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.340
something but you don't have the time for it,

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.853
outsource it.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.856
^So per your suggestions, I'm gonna have my two kids

00:00:40.856 --> 00:00:42.440
^do my makeup for a week.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.892
My six year old and my three year old boys

00:00:44.892 --> 00:00:47.440
are going to do my makeup for a week.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.200
I think this is gonna be a disaster

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.870
but this is what you guys wanted and best case scenario,

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.710
you know, they enjoy themselves and I learn

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.840
a couple makeup tips.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.263
So wish me luck.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.270
^I have a question.

00:00:58.515 --> 00:00:59.348
^- What?

00:00:59.348 --> 00:01:00.953
^- Do you want to do my makeup today?

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.173
- Yeah.

00:01:02.173 --> 00:01:03.006
- Okay.

00:01:03.006 --> 00:01:03.839
Are you gonna do it?

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:04.703
- Yeah.

00:01:04.703 --> 00:01:06.310
- My kids' relationship with makeup thus far

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:08.891
is kind of just this mysterious thing mom has

00:01:08.891 --> 00:01:11.050
in her purse that you're not allowed to touch

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:13.159
so you really want to touch it and like,

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:14.880
make a huge mess of it.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.253
Like gum.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.250
I can't even tell you how many times Wyatt has taken my

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.020
Colourpop liquid matte lipstick and put it on himself

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.100
and then lost the tube.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.240
They're probably under a random piece of furniture

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.253
just like slowly staining everything because

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.530
if anybody owns that you know how much it gets

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.420
all over everything and it does not come off.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.730
I didn't really give my kids any guidelines,

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.860
I just kind of spread it out like a big smorgasbord

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.660
but I realized very quickly that that was not

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.960
the way I should have approached things

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.900
because all they did was take their makeup brushes

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.450
and mix every single makeup that was out there

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.303
together and just pile it all over my face.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.090
It's like when you're a little kid in a restaurant

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.810
and you have a fountain drink cup and you decide

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.490
to get a little bit of every flavor because

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.303
it seems like a cool idea but it actually tastes

00:01:58.303 --> 00:01:59.440
really bad.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.440
That's basically how the first day went.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.810
^Okay so this is me ready for the day.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.053
That's concealer.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:09.440
And they did my eyebrows and mascara and eyeshadow

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:10.783
and blush.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.210
Didn't really blend my concealer and

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.410
my lips.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.950
You guys happy with your work?

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:18.783
- Yeah.

00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:20.330
- It's really funny because I didn't give anyone

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.130
a heads up on this experiment but the second I walked

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.360
into work, everyone was like,

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.460
Do you like my makeup?

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.830
- Looks like someone special put it on you.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:29.553
Your children?

00:02:29.553 --> 00:02:30.386
Your sons?

00:02:30.608 --> 00:02:31.441
- Everybody knows.

00:02:31.441 --> 00:02:33.543
Can you guess who did the lipstick?

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:34.683
- Wyatt.

00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:35.516
- Yeah.

00:02:35.516 --> 00:02:38.523
^We are trying a makeup look today that is called

00:02:38.523 --> 00:02:40.740
"high school dance".

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.303
That's what the boys picked.

00:02:42.436 --> 00:02:44.930
I'm hoping that when they're done I'm gonna look

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.090
ready for homecoming.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:49.023
I have my coffee, oh you're cool,

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:52.830
and a whole spread of makeup out and ready

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.010
for them to use.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.211
So are you guys ready to do it?

00:02:55.211 --> 00:02:56.211
- Yes!
- Yay!

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.353
- Yay!

00:02:57.353 --> 00:02:59.930
- We decided that I was gonna pull up a list of

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.330
different makeup looks and they'd get to choose one.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.754
I'd pull up an image of what it looked like and then

00:03:04.754 --> 00:03:08.040
show them the brush and the shade they would use

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.018
to achieve that and then they took that

00:03:10.018 --> 00:03:11.210
and ran with it.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:14.896
And it went a lot smoother as far as not ruining

00:03:14.896 --> 00:03:17.513
all the makeup I'd just bought but they're not,

00:03:17.513 --> 00:03:21.300
they're just not good at doing makeup?

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.830
This was a look with a lot of heavy eyeshadow,

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:28.140
highlighter, lots of blush, pretty lips

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.740
but they were doing it at like, 8:30 in the morning

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.200
so it looked very ridiculous.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.303
^This is my homecoming look!

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.913
This went a lot worse than I thought it would.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.657
I don't wanna leave the house.

00:03:43.547 --> 00:03:47.230
Really did not think it could look this bad but

00:03:47.561 --> 00:03:48.394
here we are.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.663
Get your pants on, okay.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.363
Go get your pants on.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:55.520
^Today we're gonna do a natural look because I feel

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.490
like less makeup is better.

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.340
Do you know how to do a natural look?

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:01.300
- Yes.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.420
- I chose a natural makeup look because there is

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.000
only so much you can mess up with nude eyeshadow

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.373
and it really don't show.

00:04:08.135 --> 00:04:08.983
Wow.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.700
So I just needed a little break from the intensity

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:15.030
and also my skin needed a break.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.890
I was getting very irritated eyes and I figured

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.890
this would give them a chance to adjust.

00:04:22.422 --> 00:04:23.583
Mmm!

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.570
Thank you, you did a good job.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:27.890
^Here's my completed natural look.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.740
^The lips are a little bare, like the corners

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.100
were not completely done.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:36.850
I don't know if Wyatt was going for a 20's flapper look

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:39.350
but the eyeshadow colors are pretty good.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:43.260
I really think the natural look is the best look so far

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.313
because there was less for them to mess up.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.923
I did ask Matt how he thought the makeup looked.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.090
^- You look beautiful.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.300
^Just gorgeous.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.938
- And he could not tell the difference between

00:04:53.938 --> 00:04:57.050
the way I do my makeup and the way the kids

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.069
did my makeup which, I think says something about

00:05:00.069 --> 00:05:02.287
my makeup abilities.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.733
^So I think we're gonna do a smokey eye.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:06.103
^- Yes!

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.663
And lipstick.

00:05:09.663 --> 00:05:10.650
- And lipstick.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.314
Are you guys getting better at this?

00:05:12.314 --> 00:05:13.462
- Yes!

00:05:13.462 --> 00:05:14.610
- Yeah.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:16.263
I don't know about that.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.330
I don't know what it is with kids instincts,

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.697
they just want the darkest most ugh,

00:05:21.428 --> 00:05:24.330
noticeable thing, they were just itching

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:25.783
to use the dark colors.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.883
- First I'm gonna put this makeup on my mom.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.300
- And they were dying to use my eyeliner.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.050
There were some things that I just didn't

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:36.080
have them use one of which was my eyeliner pen

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.330
because I didn't want to lose an eye.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.840
I didn't want that in a two year old's hands anywhere

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:43.793
near my face.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.473
Oh, ow ow ow.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.343
Oh my god.

00:05:46.343 --> 00:05:48.960
So I caved this time and I let them use the eyeliner.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.130
So Jackson is in charge of doing the eyeliner

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:54.543
and I totally understand what happened with him.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.530
^Jackson started doing the eyeliner and was kind of

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.823
^of those things like,

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.810
I can relate when you're doing your winged eyeliner

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:04.960
and you get a part wrong and you end up just making

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.140
it thicker and thicker and thicker until it's covering

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.950
your entire eye, that's kind of what happened here.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:13.093
It happens to grown women, I can't fault him for it.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.800
It was a solid effort.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.743
I look like I slept in my makeup.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.193
Oh my god, I do not want to go out like this.

00:06:22.821 --> 00:06:24.270
Can I just wear my sunglasses all day?

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.223
- Might be a little bit of a cop out if you agreed

00:06:26.223 --> 00:06:29.013
for them to do your makeup all week.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:32.610
- This day got a lot more reactions than the first

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.450
day I had gone to work with the makeup.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.773
- Why are you wearing, oh.

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:39.920
- I walked out to meet Nick to go to lunch

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.260
and his immediate reaction was like,

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.263
^- Where are you going?

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.430
^You're not going to lunch looking like that.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:46.310
- [Hannah] Yes we are!

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:47.307
- Why?!

00:06:47.351 --> 00:06:48.184
I can't.

00:06:48.431 --> 00:06:49.264
Cannot.

00:06:49.684 --> 00:06:51.100
^- I wanna do rock and roll!

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.780
^- You want to do rock and roll high school?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.600
They kept asking to do rock and roll high school makeup

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.793
because they're obsessed with The Ramones?

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:59.083
What is that?

00:06:59.365 --> 00:07:00.198
- A song!

00:07:00.198 --> 00:07:01.031
- [Hannah] It's a song?

00:07:01.031 --> 00:07:04.233
Wanna do a makeup look based on rock and roll high school?

00:07:04.264 --> 00:07:05.097
- Yes.

00:07:05.097 --> 00:07:05.930
- Kay.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.833
We'll see how that turns out.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:11.851
It's like, you know when kids throw out arbitrary

00:07:11.851 --> 00:07:13.907
phrases for stuff where they're like

00:07:13.907 --> 00:07:16.570
"I want Spider-Man waffles" and I'm like we don't

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:19.320
have, what constitutes a Spider-Man waffle?

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:23.480
I don't know if these are meant to be second eyebrows

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.903
or eyeliner but they're there.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:29.550
You can't really see how much eyeshadow is

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.650
dusted under here and I'm afraid to touch it

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:33.975
because I feel like it's all gonna smear

00:07:33.975 --> 00:07:36.841
but this was the first day that they started actually

00:07:36.841 --> 00:07:39.617
asking me "where does this go?"

00:07:39.617 --> 00:07:40.507
"Where do I put this?"

00:07:40.507 --> 00:07:41.530
"How do I blend it?"

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:44.580
and they were super into learning the intricacies

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:45.703
of doing makeup.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:48.600
Wyatt will even take a little makeup,

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:50.070
like a little eyeshadow on the brush

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.370
and hold it up and be like

00:07:51.395 --> 00:07:52.407
(blowing)

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.683
and then put it on me.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:56.543
It was so funny to see them do it.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.110
^I don't know, if I'm looking like this everywhere

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:03.150
^you can't really tell but also my face overall looks

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:05.693
a lot pinker than the rest of my body.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.830
But if I go like this, if I walk around like this all day

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:10.143
no one will notice.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.423
^Today is glitter day.

00:08:12.643 --> 00:08:13.476
^- Yeah.

00:08:13.476 --> 00:08:14.309
^- Okay.

00:08:14.551 --> 00:08:15.468
- Princess.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.343
- Alright, lets do it.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:19.280
They had also been eyeing the sparkle eyeshadows

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.573
for a very long time and the highlighter that I bought.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:27.660
They did a My Little Pony glitter princess highlighter

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.350
all over my entire face makeup look.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.890
Look at that brush.

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:34.610
This brush is a glitter forest.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:37.300
^I don't know if you can tell, there's glitter everywhere

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:40.750
^and Wyatt kind of painted

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:43.630
the sides of my face

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:48.453
and today is the day I have to go grocery shopping.

00:08:48.889 --> 00:08:49.722
- Yay!

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:51.390
- I love grocery shopping.

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:53.911
It's like my happy place, my special time

00:08:53.911 --> 00:08:57.683
and I really didn't want to go in this makeup.

00:08:57.723 --> 00:09:01.793
That is some shiny all over my face.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.093
Even above my mouth.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.333
Alright, here goes nothing.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:08.453
We're going in.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.245
I didn't want to risk not being able to go back

00:09:11.245 --> 00:09:13.900
to that Trader Joe's out of embarrassment and I didn't

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.792
want to risk being known as the woman with

00:09:15.792 --> 00:09:18.043
the weird makeup.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:19.963
This is so embarrassing.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:25.193
Every time I blink there's a glitter puff that flies off.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:27.630
The cashier was super nice to me.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.990
I know they were probably like holding in their

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:32.330
laughter the entire time but they were very kind

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:35.170
and I got through the entire shopping experience

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.880
unscathed for the most part.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.120
^So today we're doing fancy makeup.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:40.900
^I don't quite know what that means but Wyatt's

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:42.213
gonna take the lead.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:45.930
Apparently what it means is blue and green eyeshadow

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:47.173
to match my hair.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:50.460
Which is, it's cute in theory but they were trying

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:54.380
to do some under eye shadow that ended up just

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.984
kind of circling the bottom and making me look like I

00:09:56.984 --> 00:10:00.330
had been punched in both eyes and then Jackson

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:02.857
who had been practicing this whole week was like

00:10:02.857 --> 00:10:03.940
"I want to do your lipstick!"

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:06.363
and he whips out my LipSense.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:11.022
The second he pulled out the wand, I had flashes of

00:10:11.022 --> 00:10:13.880
the Joker makeup stuck on my face.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.580
He actually did a really good job and I'm super

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:17.810
super grateful.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:20.990
^I guess fancy makeup means blues and greens and very

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:22.883
very bright red lipstick.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.190
I'm gonna add a little mascara to this.

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:27.145
I just, I can't have them do it because

00:10:27.145 --> 00:10:28.427
there is the,

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:30.060
- [Wyatt] I do mascara.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:31.080
- You can help me.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.488
Overall from here down I looked okay and then

00:10:33.488 --> 00:10:35.820
from here up I looked like I'd gotten in

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.163
a severe fist fight.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:40.144
So I got to work that day and really of all the days

00:10:40.144 --> 00:10:45.030
this day had the most at stake because there was

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:48.360
a meeting with my team and some clients calling

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:49.403
in on video chat.

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:50.933
So I told myself it's on video,

00:10:50.933 --> 00:10:53.340
they're not gonna be able to see very well.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.573
It's gonna be blurry.

00:10:54.739 --> 00:10:57.990
But then my coworker walked in and all that immediately

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.593
went down the drain.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.593
^- We have clients at this meeting.

00:11:02.648 --> 00:11:04.390
^It looks like you got punched in the eye.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.940
- [Hannah] They're not gonna see because it's on video.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:07.773
- No.

00:11:07.773 --> 00:11:09.050
You need to take that off.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:11.693
- I have a solution for this.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:14.620
So I probably looked super hungover but after

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:17.230
seven days of this experiment I'd much rather

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:20.223
look hungover than like a crazy makeup lady.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:22.520
So what did I learn from this seven days

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:23.620
of complete madness?

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.420
Well first I learned that I could afford to spend

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:28.440
^a little more time on my makeup in the morning.

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.700
There's a lot of stuff that I could try and it really

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:33.810
doesn't take that long to do something fun and unique

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:36.620
with makeup and actually put a little bit of effort into it

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:37.800
and it's fun!

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.930
I want to do more of it and I want to try more.

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:43.290
Second I learned that my kids, bless their hearts,

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:45.880
^they think I'm beautiful no matter what.

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:48.760
Through this whole experiment every day no matter

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:51.440
how horrendous my makeup looked they would be

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.594
constantly encouraging me, constantly telling me

00:11:53.594 --> 00:11:56.840
how beautiful I am and how awesome I am and how

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:57.733
great I looked.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:58.778
- Pretty mom.

00:11:58.778 --> 00:12:02.393
- You're so pretty you look like mermaid.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:06.000
- It was so nice to just see that what's on the surface

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.437
is not what they see, they just genuinely love me a lot

00:12:09.437 --> 00:12:10.750
and I love them a lot.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.260
They're happy with me no matter how I look.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:15.670
^And third, I realized that my kids likely will

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.530
^never be makeup artists, not in the near future,

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:19.563
not ever.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.092
Probably not even artists but you know,

00:12:22.092 --> 00:12:23.250
that's okay.

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:26.713
Go be an athlete, go be a scientist, go be an engineer,

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:29.510
pay for my nice nursing home, love you, thanks,

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:30.683
remember your mom.

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:33.923
Just don't do my makeup or anyone else's.

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:40.420
Alright guys, I did it.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:43.943
Go easy on me because I'm still a beginner but I did it.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:45.780
Anyway that's all I've got for today.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.710
I'm Hannah and I learned a lot in this experiment

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:51.010
but I've got to know, have you guys ever let your kids

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:51.859
do your makeup?

00:12:51.859 --> 00:12:54.359
Or are you gonna let your kids do your makeup because

00:12:54.359 --> 00:12:56.600
if so, leave it in the comments,

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:58.590
I really wanna know that I'm not alone.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.660
And if you really want to make my day,

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:03.023
^text me a picture of how it looks.

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:05.750
^This is a real number and I read every single one

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.730
^and I would love to see what your kids come up with

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.843
^because hopefully it's better than what my kids did.

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:13.720
Now if you'll excuse me, I have to get out of the house

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:16.401
because I have makeup on today and I need

00:13:16.401 --> 00:13:17.888
somebody to see it even if it's just

00:13:17.888 --> 00:13:19.743
my grocery store cashier.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:20.663
Till next time!

00:13:22.341 --> 00:13:24.924
(cheery music)

00:13:36.086 --> 00:13:38.137
^Thank god there's a mouth hole on this.

